A||||10||ArchMagi||Windows||||5||
Z||000000||ArchMagi||02-23-2001||09:50 PM||||Does anyone make a P/W kit?  Found a great car but both the windows are shot.<P>Thanks||||reg||5
Z||000001||MrPBody||02-24-2001||04:10 PM||||According to a guy who does this often (not me) -- the best way to install power windows is to replace the doors.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||02-24-2001||04:36 PM||||As far as I know, nobody makes a kit for the Fiero however there are a some companies that make kits you can make fit, check out some street rod venders.  Best way to add P/W's would be from a donor Fiero, that's how I added power windows to my Fiero.<P>You don't necessarily have to replace the doors.  You can remove the window regulator by punching out the rivets that hold it to the door.  Of course you'll need a "Big Daddy" rivet gun and large rivets to put the regulator back in.  You'll also need the wiring, switches, etc. from a donor car.  The holes and everything for the P/W's are already stamped in the door.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ArchMagi||02-27-2001||01:42 AM||||The power windows are installed allread, they just dont work.  So as i see it, several things could be wrong<P>motor, electrical, etc...<P>if its only a motor, are they hard to install? woulden't immagine they are. plus, where could i get one.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||MontanaFiero||02-27-2001||03:14 AM||||Don't try to do it by changing the regulators, that was the MOST frustrating thing I have ever attempted with this car. It is also the reason my '87 coupe has one roll down window and one electric window.<P><BR>As soon as it warms up I will be changing the passenger DOOR. Much easier.<P>------------------<BR>&gt;&gt; '87 Coupe 4 cyl, auto &lt;&lt;<BR>&gt;&gt; '86 SE V6, 4 speed- <I>project</I> &lt;&lt;||||reg||1
Z||000005||gabriel||02-27-2001||04:44 AM||||Just replacing the WINDOW on my drivers side had me cursing the Pontiac engineers for days, let alone retrofitting PW into the door!  (I have PW)<P>  Looking at the door, it seems to me that they sort of built/assembled the door structure *around* the window by riveting the frame parts together after placing the window in the channel.<P>  How they ever concieved that anyone could replace the glass is beyond me, outside of having some specialty tools that prolly cost $$$$$$$$, and are good for nothing else.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>  However, I am sure that was a cost efficient method of assembly. (and I did get the window in.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)<P>   I would replace the door.  You can always retain the skins to avoid having to repaint.<P>   But like, if you decide to go for it & install PW, make sure you post some pics of your method of installation!<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000006||gabriel||02-27-2001||06:00 AM||||Oh, BTW, here is a site that has power-everything for your Fiero. Windows, locks, latches, etc:<P>      <A HREF="http://www.gscustom.com/power.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gscustom.com/power.htm</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||2xsess||02-27-2001||07:11 AM||||It's pretty easy to test to see if the motor is good or not, simply unplug the wiring harness at the motor and use leads connected to a battery and touch them on the connector on the motor, if it goes up and down tehn your problem lies elsewhere.<P>I'd say change the doors, It took me and my dad about 7 hours of messing around with my old 88GT just to get it near right. And it was a P/W car.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>AOL IM : Only2xsess<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2xsess.gif">      <BR> <A HREF="http://kresgeus.homestead.com/FieroPage.html" TARGET=_blank>Visit My Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carrolles||02-28-2001||07:59 AM||||There are alternatives to re-installing the rivets to mount the PW actuators.  However Harbor Freight sells the LARGE HAND RIVETER for around $15 US which includes 25 of each of 4 size rivets (1/4" included).<P>It could be that your switches are bad or that the power connector or circuit breaker are shot.  Don't give up without checking out the circuit.<p>[This message has been edited by Carrolles (edited 02-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||stimpy||02-28-2001||11:17 AM||||JC Whitney sells a universal kit to change from manual to power windows. Mounts a small motor on the regulator. A guy who came to our show last year from TX had them in his car and it came out very smooth.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Indiana_resto_guy||02-28-2001||04:37 PM||||Ever think of checking the circut breaker for good contact or even if it's any good?||||reg||1
